{"timestamp": 1779377226.843311, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 15, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779377232.155374, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I found Eve's body here in security when I arrived. My route was electrical \u2192 medbay \u2192 storage \u2192 navigation \u2192 security. I saw Frank in medbay early on at tick 2, and Charlie was alive in storage around tick 6-7, coming in from lower engine. So Charlie and Frank were both alive when I saw them. Since Charlie is also dead now, whoever killed Eve and Charlie had to be moving around \u2014 I'd really like to hear Frank, Alice, and Bob's routes, especially anyone who was near security or wherever Charlie ended up."}}
{"timestamp": 1779377238.716958, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I started in security where I saw Eve come in from weapons around tick 4-5. I left security and went weapons \u2192 cafeteria \u2192 medbay \u2192 electrical. I saw Charlie in medbay around tick 13, alive, and then I continued to electrical where I was when the meeting was called.\n\nSo Eve was alive in security when I left her there, and Charlie was alive in medbay at tick 13. Diana, you said you arrived in security and found Eve's body \u2014 what tick was that? Because if Eve was killed in security after I left, I want to know who else passed through there. And Charlie being in medbay at 13 means he was killed somewhere after that, pretty recently.\n\nI'd really like to hear Frank and Alice's routes \u2014 especially anyone who was in security after tick 5 or in medbay/storage after tick 13."}}
{"timestamp": 1779377247.328543, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "My route was cafeteria \u2192 medbay \u2192 electrical \u2192 medbay \u2192 cafeteria \u2192 weapons, and I ended up in weapons when the meeting was called. I saw Diana in medbay at tick 2, which matches what she said about seeing me there.\n\nI didn't see Eve, Charlie, Alice, or Bob at any point during my route. That's a bit odd because Bob says he went through medbay and electrical, and I was bouncing between those rooms \u2014 but our timings could have just missed each other if he was there around tick 13 and I'd already left medbay by then heading to cafeteria/weapons.\n\nWhat stands out to me: Diana's route ends at security where she found Eve's body, and Bob says he left Eve alive in security. So either Eve was killed shortly after Bob left, or Diana is lying about finding the body. Diana also vouches for me being in medbay at tick 2, which is true.\n\nI haven't heard from Alice yet \u2014 she's the only one completely unaccounted for. I'd really like to hear her route before voting. Right now my lean is Alice, but I want to hear her out first."}}
{"timestamp": 1779377260.1119518, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "My route was oxygen \u2192 upper engine \u2192 lower engine, and then I was respawned to storage when the meeting was called. I was doing tasks the whole time and honestly didn't see a single other player \u2014 I was on the west side of the map the entire round while everyone else seems to have been clustered around cafeteria/medbay/electrical/security.\n\nI know that makes my alibi unverifiable, which is frustrating, but let me work with what we have:\n\n- Diana found Eve's body in security. Bob says he left Eve alive in security and went weapons \u2192 cafeteria \u2192 medbay \u2192 electrical.\n- Frank's route bounced medbay/electrical/cafeteria/weapons.\n- Charlie was seen alive in storage (Diana, ~tick 6-7) and medbay (Bob, ~tick 13).\n\nThe key question: who killed Eve in security after Bob left, AND killed Charlie after tick 13? Bob ends in electrical. Frank ends in weapons \u2014 and weapons connects directly to security. Frank also claims he never saw Bob or Charlie despite them allegedly overlapping in medbay/electrical area, which is a little convenient.\n\nDiana's route ending at the body is normal for a reporter. Bob's story is internally consistent and gives Frank no alibi. Frank ending in weapons (adjacent to security) is suspicious given Eve died in security.\n\nI'm leaning Frank. I was nowhere near any of this and have no motive to push a wrong vote. If I'm wrong, I'd rather skip than lynch Diana or Bob who have given concrete cross-referenced info.\n\nMy vote: Frank."}}
{"timestamp": 1779377269.218119, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I arrived at security at tick 14 and found Eve's body immediately \u2014 that's when I called the meeting. To clarify my timeline: electrical early, medbay around tick 2 (saw Frank), storage tick 6-7 (saw Charlie come in from lower engine), then navigation, then security where I found Eve.\n\nListening to everyone now: Bob and Frank's stories partially cross-reference each other through medbay/electrical, though Frank says he didn't see Bob which is a little odd. Alice was on the west side alone \u2014 unverifiable but consistent with being away from both murder scenes.\n\nAlice makes a strong point about Frank ending in weapons, which is directly adjacent to security where Eve died. That's the room you'd retreat to after a security kill. And Charlie being last seen in medbay at tick 13 (per Bob) means whoever killed him was in that area recently \u2014 Frank was bouncing through medbay/electrical/cafeteria.\n\nBob's route is linear and ends in electrical, far from security. Frank's route is the only one that puts him adjacent to security at the end AND in medbay near Charlie's last known location.\n\nI'm leaning Frank too, but I want to hear if Bob has anything to add about whether he saw Frank in medbay or electrical during their alleged overlap."}}
{"timestamp": 1779377279.789541, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Good question Diana \u2014 let me address that directly. I did NOT see Frank in medbay or electrical during my route. I was in medbay around tick 12-13 and saw Charlie there, but no Frank. I went straight to electrical after that and was alone there until the meeting.\n\nSo Frank claims he was bouncing medbay \u2192 electrical \u2192 medbay \u2192 cafeteria \u2192 weapons, but our paths should have crossed somewhere in that medbay/electrical corridor and they didn't. He says \"our timings could have just missed each other\" \u2014 maybe, but it's convenient.\n\nWhat's damning for me:\n- Frank ends in weapons, one room from security where Eve died.\n- Frank was in the medbay/electrical cluster where Charlie was last seen alive (by me, tick 13).\n- Frank's route has him criss-crossing the exact rooms where both victims were, but he conveniently saw nobody.\n- Alice was demonstrably on the west side (oxygen/upper engine/lower engine) \u2014 those rooms are far from both crime scenes.\n\nDiana found the body and her timeline cross-references with multiple people. I left Eve alive in security and went the opposite direction. Alice was isolated west. Frank is the only one whose route covers both murder locations with the timing to do it.\n\nMy vote is Frank."}}
{"timestamp": 1779377294.011452, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Okay, I need to defend myself here because the case against me is circumstantial but it's stacking up.\n\nLet me address the key points:\n\n1. **Weapons being adjacent to security**: Yes, I ended in weapons. But weapons is also adjacent to cafeteria, which is where I came from. My route makes sense \u2014 I was doing tasks. If I killed Eve in security, why would I then walk AWAY from the body into weapons rather than reporting it myself to deflect suspicion? Killers don't usually sit next door to their victim.\n\n2. **Not seeing Bob in medbay/electrical**: Bob says he was in medbay around tick 12-13. I was in medbay early (tick 2 with Diana), then electrical, then BACK through medbay earlier than that, then cafeteria, then weapons. By tick 12-13 I was likely already in cafeteria or weapons. Our paths genuinely could have missed \u2014 I was moving west-to-east-to-west-to-east, he was moving east-to-west linearly.\n\n3. **Charlie's death**: Bob is the LAST person to see Charlie alive in medbay at tick 13. That's just as suspicious as anything about me. Bob then claims he went to electrical and was \"alone there until the meeting.\" Convenient \u2014 no witnesses for the back half of his route either.\n\n4. **Diana vouches for me at tick 2**. That's confirmed.\n\nHere's what bothers me: Bob's story has him being the last to see BOTH victims alive (Eve in security at tick 4-5, Charlie in medbay at tick 13). That's a bigger red flag than my route covering rooms.\n\nAlice's west-side route is completely unverifiable. Could go either way.\n\nI'm not going to vote Alice on no evidence. Between Bob and me, I know I'm innocent. I'm voting **Bob** \u2014 he's the common thread to both victims' last known sightings."}}
{"timestamp": 1779377306.530089, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I've already spoken once this round \u2014 Frank is now trying to flip it on Bob, which is exactly what I'd expect from someone cornered.\n\nLet me address Frank's defense:\n\n1. \"Why would I walk away from the body into weapons?\" \u2014 Because weapons is a task room and it looks natural. Sitting on the body would be worse. That's not exonerating, it's just route optimization.\n\n2. The \"missed each other\" excuse for not seeing Bob: Frank claims he bounced medbay \u2192 electrical \u2192 medbay \u2192 cafeteria \u2192 weapons. Bob was in medbay at tick 12-13 then electrical until the meeting (tick 15). For Frank's story to work, he had to clear out of both medbay AND electrical before Bob arrived. That's a tight squeeze with a lot of back-and-forth that conveniently leaves no witnesses.\n\n3. Frank pointing at Bob as \"last to see both victims\": Bob saw Eve in security and LEFT going weapons \u2192 cafeteria \u2192 medbay \u2192 electrical. That's a linear path away from security. Frank's route ends ADJACENT to security after looping back east. Frank had opportunity for both kills; Bob's linear route makes the Eve kill geographically awkward.\n\n4. Diana cross-references with both Frank (medbay tick 2) and Bob. Bob's route is linear and verifiable in pieces. Frank's is a chaotic loop that conveniently misses everyone.\n\nThe cleanest read: Diana = confirmed reporter with consistent timeline. Bob = linear route away from Eve. Me = isolated west, no opportunity. Frank = bouncing through every relevant room, ending adjacent to the body, seeing nobody.\n\n**My vote stays Frank.**"}}
